-- title:
--   Determinant is cyclotomic from Frobenius determinants
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring and let $\rho$ be an element of [`GaloisRepAdic A`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16): a type $V$ carrying the structure of a finite free $A$-module of rank $2$ (its $A$-rank being asserted to equal $2$), together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho.\rho$ from the group of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` to $\mathrm{End}_A(V)$ which is adically continuous in the sense that for every $n$ there is an intermediate field $L$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that every automorphism fixing $L$ pointwise moves each $v \in V$ into $\mathfrak{m}^n \cdot V$, where $\mathfrak{m}$ is the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $p$ be a prime whose image in $A$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}$, and let $S$ be a finite set of naturals. Assume that for every prime $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $B$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $(\ell : \overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ a non-unit of $B$, and every automorphism $\tau$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acting on the residue field of $B$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, one has $\det \rho.\rho(\tau) = (\ell : A)$. The conclusion is `ρ.DetIsCyclotomic p`: the image of $p$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}$, and for all $n$, all automorphisms $\sigma$ and all $a \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $\sigma\mu = \mu^a$ for every $\mu \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\mu^{p^n} = 1$, the element $\det \rho.\rho(\sigma) - (a : A)$ lies in the ideal of $A$ generated by $p^n$.
--
--   This is the standard identification of the determinant of a two-dimensional $p$-adic Galois representation with the $p$-adic cyclotomic character, deduced from the values of the determinant at Frobenius elements outside a finite set of primes by density of Frobenius conjugacy classes. It is used to verify the determinant condition for the representations attached to Hecke-side constructions and to elliptic curves, and is invoked at many places in the cohomological and Hecke-algebra parts of the development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRepAdic_detIsCyclotomic_of_forall_frobenius_det_eq.lean

import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_LocalConditions

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem GaloisRepAdic.detIsCyclotomic_of_forall_frobenius_det_eq
    {A : Type} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (ρ : GaloisRepAdic A)
    {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hpA : (p : A) ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (S : Finset ℕ)
    (hdet : ∀ ℓ : ℕ, ℓ.Prime → ℓ ∉ S → ∀ (B : ValuationSubring (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))
      (τ : AlgebraicClosure ℚ ≃ₐ[ℚ] AlgebraicClosure ℚ), B.LiesOverPrime ℓ → B.IsFrobeniusAt τ ℓ →
        LinearMap.det (ρ.ρ τ) = (ℓ : A)) :
    ρ.DetIsCyclotomic p := by sorry
